9 j.","Kinderen 9-12 j."]}},"educational_targets":{"list":[],"translations":{}},"tags":["kids"]},{"id":50013304,"date_start":"2024-10-25","date_end":"2024-10-31","date_next":"2024-10-28","accept_article27":false,"accept_cultuurbon":false,"accept_paspartoe":false,"is_closed_on_public_holidays":true,"is_closed_on_school_holidays":false,"is_only_by_appointment":false,"is_permanent":false,"is_free":true,"is_pay_as_you_can":false,"is_online":false,"is_canceled":false,"is_soldout":false,"last_updated_at":"2024-10-26T03:01:06+02:00","published_at":"2024-08-09T15:50:11+02:00","publication_state":"public","date_embargo":null,"show_in_agenda":true,"is_outside":false,"is_high_capacity":false,"is_not_major_event":false,"backoffice_id":305285,"facebook_link":null,"import_origin":null,"is_part_of":null,"sub_type":"other","ranking":0.5227579585747102,"languages":{"spoken":["fr","en"],"subtitles":[]},"categories":{"main":{"id":23,"translations":{"de":"Ausstellung","pt":null,"en":"Exhibitions","it":"Esposizioni","cn":null,"fr":"Expositions","sp":"Exhibici\u00f3n","nl":"Tentoonstellingen"}},"others":{"list":[46,36],"translations":{"de":["Multidisziplin\u00e4r","Museen & Kunstzentren"],"pt":[null,null],"en":["Multidisciplinary","Museums and art centers"],"it":["Multidisciplinare","Musei e centri artistici"],"cn":[null,null],"fr":["Pluridisciplinaire","Mus\u00e9es et art centers"],"sp":["Multidisciplinar","Museos y centros de arte"],"nl":["Multidisciplinair","Musea en kunstcentra"]}}},"translations":{"de":{"name":"\"Yokai\" Exhibition by Stephan Goldrajch","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.be.emb-japan.go.jp\/itpr_en\/culture_event_jicc.html#oct2024","email":"info@bx.mofa.go.jp","phone_contact":"+32 2 513 23 40","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/de\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50013304"},"pt":{"name":"\"Yokai\" Exhibition by Stephan Goldrajch","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.be.emb-japan.go.jp\/itpr_en\/culture_event_jicc.html#oct2024","email":"info@bx.mofa.go.jp","phone_contact":"+32 2 513 23 40","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/pt\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50013304"},"en":{"name":"\"Yokai\" by Stephan Goldrajch","shortdescr":"The exhibition features Stephan Goldrajch\u2019s textile sculptures, paintings, and watercolors, created during his residency in Japan in 2023. Goldrajch\u2019s art draws inspiration from ancestral traditions, human interactions, and social cohesion. ","longdescr":"Using crochet and various threads, Goldrajch crafts vibrant, textured compositions, often incorporating wool and cotton. His work, rich in fantasy, revisits childhood memories and tales through intricate, meditative processes. Collaborating with photographer Myriam Rispens, he works across multiple disciplines, including watercolor painting, weaving, and embroidery, focusing on creating connections between people and cultures. \n\nGoldrajch's art has been exhibited in numerous international institutions, including the International Carnival and Mask Museum and the Museum of Contemporary Art in Athens. He has also had solo shows at Art Gen\u00e8ve, Art Paris, Art Brussels, and Baronian Xippas in Paris and Brussels. His residencies span China, Armenia, Bulgaria, and Benin, and he has published several books, including \"Po\u00e8me d'Arm\u00e9nie\" and \"Masques.\" \n\nGoldrajch's artistic approach emphasizes participation and interaction, often engaging with non-artists to enrich his work. His projects and performances are deeply social, aiming to build links and foster understanding between diverse groups. \n\nThe exhibition is curated by Albert Baronian. ","performers":"Stephan Goldrajch (Artist) \nMyriam Rispens (Photographer)\nAlbert Baronian (Curator)","boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.be.emb-japan.go.jp\/itpr_en\/culture_event_jicc.html#oct2024","email":"info@bx.mofa.go.jp","phone_contact":"+32 2 513 23 40","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/en\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50013304"},"it":{"name":"\"Yokai\" Exhibition by Stephan Goldrajch","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.be.emb-japan.go.jp\/itpr_en\/culture_event_jicc.html#oct2024","email":"info@bx.mofa.go.jp","phone_contact":"+32 2 513 23 40","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/it\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50013304"},"cn":{"name":"\"Yokai\" Exhibition by Stephan Goldrajch","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.be.emb-japan.go.jp\/itpr_en\/culture_event_jicc.html#oct2024","email":"info@bx.mofa.go.jp","phone_contact":"+32 2 513 23 40","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/cn\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50013304"},"fr":{"name":"\"Yokai\" par Stephan Goldrajch","shortdescr":"L'exposition pr\u00e9sente les sculptures textiles, les peintures et les aquarelles de Stephan Goldrajch, cr\u00e9\u00e9es lors de sa r\u00e9sidence au Japon en 2023. L'art de Stephan Goldrajch s'inspire des traditions ancestrales, des interactions humaines et de la coh\u00e9sion sociale. \n","longdescr":"En utilisant le crochet et divers fils, Goldrajch cr\u00e9e des compositions vibrantes et textur\u00e9es, incorporant souvent de la laine et du coton. Son travail, riche en fantaisie, revisite les souvenirs et les contes de l'enfance \u00e0 travers des processus complexes et m\u00e9ditatifs. En collaboration avec la photographe Myriam Rispens, il travaille dans plusieurs disciplines, notamment l'aquarelle, le tissage et la broderie, en se concentrant sur la cr\u00e9ation de liens entre les personnes et les cultures. \n\nLes \u0153uvres de Goldrajch ont \u00e9t\u00e9 expos\u00e9es dans de nombreuses institutions internationales, dont le Mus\u00e9e international du carnaval et du masque et le Mus\u00e9e d'art contemporain d'Ath\u00e8nes. Il a \u00e9galement particip\u00e9 \u00e0 des expositions individuelles \u00e0 Art Gen\u00e8ve, Art Paris, Art Bruxelles et Baronian Xippas \u00e0 Paris et \u00e0 Bruxelles. Il a effectu\u00e9 des r\u00e9sidences en Chine, en Arm\u00e9nie, en Bulgarie et au B\u00e9nin, et a publi\u00e9 plusieurs livres, dont \"Po\u00e8me d'Arm\u00e9nie\" et \"Masques\". \n\nL'approche artistique de Goldrajch met l'accent sur la participation et l'interaction, s'engageant souvent avec des non-artistes pour enrichir son travail. Ses projets et ses performances sont profond\u00e9ment sociaux et visent \u00e0 cr\u00e9er des liens et \u00e0 favoriser la compr\u00e9hension entre divers groupes. \n\nL'exposition est organis\u00e9e par Albert Baronian. ","performers":"Stephan Goldrajch (Artiste) \nMyriam Rispens (Photographe)\nAlbert Baronian (Curateur)","boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.be.emb-japan.go.jp\/itpr_en\/culture_event_jicc.html#oct2024","email":"info@bx.mofa.go.jp","phone_contact":"+32 2 513 23 40","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/fr\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50013304"},"sp":{"name":"\"Yokai\" Exhibition by Stephan Goldrajch","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.be.emb-japan.go.jp\/itpr_en\/culture_event_jicc.html#oct2024","email":"info@bx.mofa.go.jp","phone_contact":"+32 2 513 23 40","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/sp\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50013304"},"nl":{"name":"\"Yokai\" door Stephan Goldrajch","shortdescr":"De tentoonstelling toont Stephan Goldrajchs textielsculpturen, schilderijen en aquarellen, gemaakt tijdens zijn verblijf in Japan in 2023. Goldrajchs kunst haalt inspiratie uit voorouderlijke tradities, menselijke interacties en sociale cohesie. ","longdescr":"Met haakwerk en verschillende garens maakt Goldrajch levendige, getextureerde composities waarin hij vaak wol en katoen verwerkt. Zijn werk is rijk aan fantasie en roept jeugdherinneringen en -verhalen op door middel van ingewikkelde, meditatieve processen. In samenwerking met fotografe Myriam Rispens werkt hij in verschillende disciplines, waaronder aquarelleren, weven en borduren, waarbij hij zich richt op het cre\u00ebren van verbindingen tussen mensen en culturen. \n\nGoldrajchs kunst is tentoongesteld in verschillende internationale instellingen, waaronder het International Carnival and Mask Museum en het Museum of Contemporary Art in Athene. Hij had ook solotentoonstellingen in Art Gen\u00e8ve, Art Paris, Art Brussels en Baronian Xippas in Parijs en Brussel. Hij verbleef in China, Armeni\u00eb, Bulgarije en Benin en publiceerde verschillende boeken, waaronder \"Po\u00e8me d'Arm\u00e9nie\" en \"Masques\". \n\nGoldrajch legt in zijn artistieke benadering de nadruk op participatie en interactie, waarbij hij vaak samenwerkt met niet-kunstenaars om zijn werk te verrijken. Zijn projecten en performances zijn zeer sociaal, met als doel banden te smeden en begrip te kweken tussen verschillende groepen. \n\nDe tentoonstelling is samengesteld door Albert Baronian. ","performers":"Stephan Goldrajch (Artiest) \nMyriam Rispens (Fotograaf)\nAlbert Baronian (Curator)","boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.be.emb-japan.go.jp\/itpr_en\/culture_event_jicc.html#oct2024","email":"info@bx.mofa.go.jp","phone_contact":"+32 2 513 23 40","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/nl\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50013304"}},"place":{"id":261989,"translations":{"de":{"name":"Centre Culturel et d'information de l'Ambassade du Japon","address_street_name":"Rue Van Maerlant","address_street_number":"1","address_street_box":null,"email":null,"website":"http:\/\/www.be.emb-japan.go.jp","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1040","address_city":"Etterbeek","address_line1":"Rue Van Maerlant, 1","address_line2":"1040 Etterbeek","description_web":null,"descriptio