ngen","pt":null,"en":"Guided tours","it":"Visite guidate","cn":null,"fr":"Visites Guid\u00e9es","sp":"Visitas guiadas","nl":"Begeleide rondleidingen"}},"others":{}},"translations":{"de":{"name":"Guided Tour of the Palace of the Nation - BBN 2024","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.explore.brussels\/fr\/bbn","email":"info@explore.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 319 50 01","phone_booking":"+32 2 319 50 01","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/de\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700000985"},"pt":{"name":"Guided Tour of the Palace of the Nation - BBN 2024","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.explore.brussels\/fr\/bbn","email":"info@explore.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 319 50 01","phone_booking":"+32 2 319 50 01","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/pt\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700000985"},"en":{"name":"Guided Tour of the Palace of the Nation - BBN 2024","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":"The home of the Belgian Federal Parliament is a Neoclassical ensemble built between 1778 and 1783 as the centrepiece of the architectural composition forming the northern side of the Royal Park. It is laid out on a U-shaped plan around a courtyard and set on the axis of the central north-south path through the Park, thus closing the view from the Royal Palace. The first edifice on the site, the Palace of the Council of Brabant which was built to the design of architect Barnab\u00e9 Guimard when Brussels was part of the Austrian Netherlands, has subsequently undergone many changes and been used for different purposes. Between 1816 and 1818, the central part of the building was converted by architect Charles Vander Straeten to house the States-General of William I; the first hemicycle was destroyed by fire in 1820 and rebuilt between 1821 and 1822. Following Belgian independence in 1831, the edifice became the Federal Parliament Building. Having again been destroyed by fire in 1883, it took architect Henri Beyaert three years to reconstruct it. Today the building houses several Belgian federal institutions, including the Chamber of Representatives and the Senate. \n\nThe visits are accessible to wheelchair users.\n\nPLEASE NOTE: For reasons of security, individual, named reservations are required. The list of visit participants will be shared with the Parliament's administrative staff and access will only be granted upon presentation of an ID card\/passport. Please arrive a few minutes before the start of your visit to allow for security checks. Please note that the entrance to be used is not the one across from the Royal Park, but rather the one located at 13, Rue de Louvain.","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.explore.brussels\/en\/bbn","email":"info@explore.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 319 50 01","phone_booking":"+32 2 319 50 01","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/en\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700000985"},"it":{"name":"Guided Tour of the Palace of the Nation - BBN 2024","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.explore.brussels\/fr\/bbn","email":"info@explore.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 319 50 01","phone_booking":"+32 2 319 50 01","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/it\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700000985"},"cn":{"name":"Guided Tour of the Palace of the Nation - BBN 2024","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.explore.brussels\/fr\/bbn","email":"info@explore.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 319 50 01","phone_booking":"+32 2 319 50 01","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/cn\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700000985"},"fr":{"name":"Visite Guid\u00e9e du Palais de la Nation - BBN 2024","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":"Le Palais de la Nation, si\u00e8ge actuel du Parlement f\u00e9d\u00e9ral belge est un ensemble n\u00e9oclassique b\u00e2ti en 1778-1783 au centre d'une composition architecturale formant le c\u00f4t\u00e9 nord du Parc royal. Reprenant la forme d'un \"U\", ax\u00e9 sur l'all\u00e9e centrale du parc et s'articulant autour d'une cour d'honneur, cet \u00e9difice ferme la perspective depuis la place des Palais. Le premier b\u00e2timent, nomm\u00e9 \"Palais du Conseil du Brabant\", fut construit durant l'occupation des Pays-Bas autrichiens, selon les plans de l'architecte Barnab\u00e9 Guimard et connut de nombreux am\u00e9nagements et affectations successives. Le corps central de l'\u00e9difice fut transform\u00e9 en 1816-1818 par l'architecte Charles Vander Straeten pour y abriter les \u00c9tats G\u00e9n\u00e9raux de Guillaume Ier, o\u00f9 un premier h\u00e9micycle br\u00fbla en 1820 avant d'\u00eatre reconstruit en 1821-1822. En 1831, apr\u00e8s l'ind\u00e9pendance belge, le b\u00e2timent devient le Palais de la Nation. \u00c0 nouveau ravag\u00e9 par un incendie en 1883, il fallut trois ans \u00e0 l'architecte Henri Beyaert pour en assurer la reconstruction. Depuis lors, le Palais de la Nation abrite plusieurs institutions de l'\u00c9tat belges, dont la Chambre des repr\u00e9sentants et le S\u00e9nat.\n\nCes visites sont accessibles aux personnes en fauteuil roulant.\n\nATTENTION : Pour des raisons de s\u00e9curit\u00e9, les inscriptions ne pourront \u00eatre qu'individuelles et nominatives ; la liste des participants sera transmise aux gestionnaires des lieux et l'acc\u00e8s au b\u00e2timent se fera uniquement sur pr\u00e9sentation d'une pi\u00e8ce d'identit\u00e9. Merci de vous pr\u00e9senter quelques minutes avant votre visite pour les diff\u00e9rents contr\u00f4les de s\u00e9curit\u00e9. Veuillez noter que l'entr\u00e9e ne s'effectue pas en face du Parc Royal, mais bien au n\u00b013 rue de Louvain.","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.explore.brussels\/fr\/bbn","email":"info@explore.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 319 50 01","phone_booking":"+32 2 319 50 01","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/fr\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700000985"},"sp":{"name":"Guided Tour of the Palace of the Nation - BBN 2024","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.explore.brussels\/fr\/bbn","email":"info@explore.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 319 50 01","phone_booking":"+32 2 319 50 01","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/sp\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700000985"},"nl":{"name":"Rondleiding van het Paleis der Natie - BBN 2024","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":"Het Paleis der Natie, de huidige zetel van het Belgische federale parlement, is een neoklassiek complex dat tussen 1778 en 1783 gebouwd werd. Op zijn beurt maakt het deel uit van een vrij homogeen geheel van gebouwen aan de noordzijde van het Warandepark. Het U-vormige complex ligt rond een centrale binnenplaats die perfect in het verlengde ligt van de noord-zuidas van het park. Het oorspronkelijke gebouw, dat de naam Brabantse Raadspaleis droeg en dat dateert uit de periode van de Oostenrijkse Nederlanden, werd ontworpen door de architect Barnab\u00e9 Guimard. In de loop van de geschiedenis werd het verschillende keren verbouwd en kende het verschillende functies. Het centrale deel van het gebouw werd in 1816-1818 door architect Charles Vander Straeten verbouwd om er de Staten-Generaal in onder te brengen die Willem I der Nederlanden had ingesteld. Het halfrond aan de achterzijde brandde al in 1820 af, maar werd in 1821-1822 herbouwd. In 1831, vlak na de Belgische onafhankelijkheid, kreeg het gebouw de bestemming van Belgisch parlementsgebouw en werd het omgedoopt tot Paleis der Natie. In 1883 trof een nieuwe brand de Kamer en het duurde drie jaar, tot 1886, vooraleer Henri Beyaert met de heropbouw startte. Vandaag de dag huisvest het Paleis der Natie verschillende Belgische staatsinstellingen, waaronder de Belgische Kamer van Volksvertegenwoordigers en de Belgische Senaat. \n\nDeze bezoeken zijn toegankelijk voor personen in een rolstoel. \n\nLET OP: Om veiligheidsredenen dienen bij het inschrijven de namen van ALLE bezoekers te worden doorgegeven. De deelnemerslijst zal worden bezorgd aan de beheerders van de militaire site en de toegang aan de gebouwen kan enkel worden verleend aan personen die in het bezit zijn van een geldig identiteitsbewijs. In het licht van de veiligheidscontroles vragen wij u ook enkele minuten voor aanvang van het bezoek aanwezig te zijn.","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.explore.brussels\/nl\/bbn","email":"info@explore.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 319 50 01","phone_booking":"+32 2 319 50 01","agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/nl\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700000985"}},"place":{"id":279869,"translations":{"de":{"name":"Palais de la Nation","address_street_name":"Rue de Louvain","address_street_number":"13","address_street_box":null,"email":null,"website":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue de Louvain, 13","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"pt":{"name":"Palais de la Nation","address_street_name":"Rue de Louvain","address_street_number":"13","address_street_box":null,"email":null,"website":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue de Louvain, 13","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"en":{"name":"Palais de la Nation","address_street_name":"Rue de Louvain","address_street_number":"13","address_street_box":null,"email":null,"website":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Brussels","address_line1":"Rue de Louvain, 13","address_line2":"1000 Brussels","description_web":n